LANTERN REVISION 02 — SOURCE REBUILD GUIDE
Audit date: 6 October 2026
Applies to the final selected source releases named below.
Containers, Mechanisms and Lighting use the repaired r02a COMPLETE archives;
Tree Forms uses v02a. Earlier failures are retained only in the audit history.

START SAFELY
Rebuild a disposable copy of an extracted pack. The scripts overwrite outputs,
source-derived layers, manifests and some review-status labels. Keep the frozen
ZIPs unchanged. For split releases, extract all parts into the same destination;
they contribute files to one pack root. Do not nest one part inside another.

“Passed command” means that exact script stage completed. “Sampled replay” means
representative frames were rebuilt and compared with the frozen exports, not
that every frame, movie or helper was re-created. All tested art samples matched
pixel-for-pixel. This verifies offline source reconstruction, not game-engine
integration, collision, runtime performance or every operating system.

DEPENDENCIES
Python 3 with Pillow and NumPy. Beetle, Scenic and Hero also require SciPy.
Hero rendering requires Blender 4.3.2. Review movies require FFmpeg with libx264.
The audit used Python 3.12, Pillow 12.3.0, NumPy 2.3.5 and SciPy 1.17.0.

Remaining font limitation: the Scenic exporter, scene diagnostics and Hero
finishing use DejaVu Sans at the Linux path
/usr/share/fonts/truetype/dejavu/DejaVuSans.ttf; Hero finishing also uses its Bold
variant. These fonts are not bundled. A system with a different font layout
needs a configured/fallback font-path source repair before those commands are
cross-platform. Asset-frame functions generally do not require these fonts.
The three repaired props packs use configurable/fallback fonts: set
LANTERN_FONT_PATH to a font file, or default for Pillow's bundled font. Their
preferred-font commands and explicit bundled-font fallback smoke test passed.
Pillow >=10.1 is recommended for size-aware fallback; typography can vary.

